@startuml holler-2-message-lifecycle
title The life of one message, from show() to gone

skinparam shadowing false
hide footbox
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
autonumber

actor "Your code" as caller
participant "Holler" as holler
participant "HollerEntry" as entry
participant "HollerHost" as host
participant "message lambda\n(your app)" as lambda
participant "HollerMessage" as message
participant "HollerCard\n+ HollerTimer" as card

== Show ==

caller -> holler : show(value, key)
holler -> entry : create, stage = Queued
holler --> caller : HollerHandle
note right of caller
    The call returns at once.
    Nothing is drawn yet.
end note

== Draw (when the message is among the first maxVisible) ==

host -> holler : read the queue
host -> entry : markShown(), stage = Visible
host -> lambda : message(value)
note over host, lambda
    A text message skips the lambda:
    the host calls HollerMessage itself.
end note
lambda -> message : HollerMessage(title, …, animation)
message -> card : draw inside the enter animation
card -> card : start the timer

== Close (time is up, close button, swipe, an action, or dismiss from code) ==

card -> entry : dismiss(reason), stage = Leaving
entry --> caller : awaitDismiss() returns the reason
message -> card : play the exit animation
host -> holler : remove the entry once the exit has ended
note over holler, host
    The next queued message, if any,
    now becomes visible and its timer starts.
end note

== Replace (show with a key that is still alive) ==

caller -> holler : show(newValue, sameKey)
holler -> entry : swap(content), same entry and place
entry --> caller : earlier awaitDismiss() returns Replaced
host -> lambda : message(newValue)
lambda -> message : HollerMessage(…)
message -> card : new card, timer starts over,\nno exit or enter animation

@enduml
